## Source of truth

```text
tasks/** spec (status + depends_on + evidence)  →  Linear issue (mirror)
```

Never mark a Linear issue **Done** without **user approval** (see § Done approval gate). Disk proof (`tasks/evidence/`, `task-verifier`) moves issues to **In Review** only — not Done. Never reorder Todo to match gut feel — use **implementation order** below.

## Board workflow (only these columns)

| Column | When | Sort |
|--------|------|------|
| **Todo** | Ready, not started | **Manual** — top = next to implement |
| **In Progress** | Active agent/dev (max 1–3) | By priority |
| **In Review** | PR open / awaiting merge | **Manual** — implementation order; **~10 active items near top** |
| **Done** | **User-approved** only — merged + verified | Closed |

Flow: **Todo → In Progress → In Review → Done** (Done requires explicit user approval; no agent/script skip).

## Done approval gate (hard rule)

**Only the user** may move an issue to **Done**. Playbook: [`tasks/linear/04-completion-approval.md`](../../../tasks/linear/04-completion-approval.md).

| Actor | When evidence passes | Linear state |
|-------|----------------------|--------------|
| Agent / script | task-verifier + evidence file | **In Review** + comment with evidence path |
| User | Reviews evidence, approves | **Done** |
| User (batch) | Adds label `approved-done` | Agent may set Done in same session if user asked |

Import scripts map disk `status: Done` → **In Review**, never Done.

Remove or hide extra statuses (Backlog, Triage, Canceled duplicates) on the MDEAPP project board.

